<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Mughan Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1919 CE · capital Lankaran</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Soviet republic proclaimed for a few weeks in 1919 by Bolsheviks among the Russian settlers of the Mughan steppe in south-eastern Azerbaijan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In spring 1919 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/provisional-military-dictatorship-of-mughan">Provisional Military Dictatorship of Mughan</a> was overthrown when a congress of local settlers, influenced by Bolsheviks, turned against the White officers who ran it. In May 1919 the congress at Lankaran proclaimed the Mughan Soviet Republic. Its leaders hoped for help from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a> across the Caspian.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was based on councils of Russian settler villages, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molokans">Molokans</a>, and sought to join <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a>. It tried to extend its control to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talysh">Talysh</a> and Azerbaijani villages, provoking fighting with local forces. Isolated and with little outside support, it never developed a stable administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In July 1919 troops of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan-democratic-republic">Azerbaijan Democratic Republic</a> and local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talysh">Talysh</a> forces captured Lankaran and ended the republic. The region came under Soviet rule with the rest of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> in 1920.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mughan-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Mughan Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lankaran</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mughan SR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=mughan-soviet-republic" aria-label="Mughan Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5892 787 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mughan Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6212 1043L6212 1043M6212 1043L6224 991"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6212 1043h0M6224 991h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6212 1043h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6212 1043h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lankaran. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=mughan-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
